<title>GERMANY: Porsche shares roar ahead.</title>
<headline>Porsche shares roar ahead.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German luxury car maker Porsche AG were among the morning's most actively traded issues, surging 4.32 percent after the group said half-year profits tripled.</p>
<p>In a mandatory bourse statement the group said its group profit climbed to 36 million marks in the first half of 1996/1997, up from 10.3 million marks in the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>The group also said it needed to expand capacities to meet demand. Shares climbed to 1,450 marks, outpacing the IBIS DAX index's 0.56 percent rise to 3,035.37 points.</p>
<p>Sales climbed by 20 percent to about 1.7 billion marks in the first half of the business year, which ends July 31.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
